# Netra Charge on iPhone (Shortcuts setup)

iPhone apps cannot listen for charging in the background, so this uses the Shortcuts app's own
automations. Setup takes about five minutes. You need the free Shortcuts app that comes with iOS.
Menu names can differ a little between iOS versions.

Apple's own steps: https://support.apple.com/guide/shortcuts/setting-triggers-apde31e9638b/ios

## The four announcements

Make four **Personal Automations**. Each one: **Shortcuts > Automation > New Automation >**
choose the trigger below **> New Blank Automation > Add Action > Speak Text**, type the phrase,
then turn **Run Immediately** on (Ask Before Running off) and turn **Notify When Run** off.

| # | Trigger | Settings | Speak Text |
|---|---------|----------|-----------|
| 1 | **Charger** | Is Connected | Connected |
| 2 | **Charger** | Is Disconnected | Disconnected |
| 3 | **Battery Level** | Rises Above 99% | Full charge |
| 4 | **Battery Level** | Falls Below 16% | Low battery |

Notes:
- Apple offers "Rises Above" and "Falls Below" for battery level, so use 99 and 16 to cover
  100% and 15%. This is the closest the Shortcuts triggers get.
- Volume and the silent switch: not verified by us. Test one announcement and adjust the volume if you hear nothing.
- Other media: we have not verified whether music pauses. Do not expect it to.
- Full charge and Low battery cannot check the charger state. Shortcuts' battery triggers only fire when the level crosses the number, so "rises above 99%" can only happen while charging and "falls below 16%" normally happens on battery. If the phone is charging and drifts down across 16%, it can still say "Low battery". Android says it only on battery.
- Rising above 99% can repeat if the level wobbles near 99 and 100. Android avoids this; Shortcuts has no way to.
- If the phone is already at 100% or below 16% when you finish setup, nothing is spoken until the next crossing (Android speaks once at start).
- Test #1 and #2 by plugging and unplugging. Test #3 and #4 only happen at those levels, so
  there is no quick test.

## Limits (honest)

- Battery Level triggers fire when the level crosses the number. If the phone is already past the level when you
  create the automation, it waits for the next crossing.
- Apple controls when automations run. They are not guaranteed in Low Power Mode or when iOS limits background work.
- This guide was written from Apple's documentation. It has not been tested on a physical iPhone by the Netra team.
